# PHP / MCP Standards

Read `docs/development/coding-standards.md` and `docs/development/security-policy.md`.

## Must

- `declare(strict_types=1);` on every PHP file
- PSR-12, native types, `final`/`readonly` where appropriate
- Env access only in `McpEnvironment`
- No secrets in code, catalogs, logs, or MCP responses
- Unit tests for behavior changes; `composer test` before PR
- Self-review: `docs/review/mcp-server.md`

## Must not

- Import NeNe/NENE2/host app code
- Add shell/filesystem MCP tools without Issue + security review
- Put bearer tokens in `tools.json` or `runtimeContext`
- Skip Issue-driven branch workflow

## Verify

```bash
composer test
```
